glyph_generation.json is FreeLab's own table of recipes for Glyph Compose's Glyph generation tab,
made by compose/train/generation.py. The recipes (how each character is built: its ways, their
operations, and their order) are FreeLab's, under FreeLab's license (GPL-3.0-or-later). It also holds:

1. From the Unicode Character Database, version 17.0.0 (https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/:
   UnicodeData.txt, NamesList.txt, confusables.txt), Copyright (c) Unicode, Inc., under the Unicode
   License V3 (below): which characters are in scope, their names, and the sources their canonical
   and compatibility decompositions name.
2. From GlyphsInfo's GlyphData.xml (https://github.com/schriftgestalt/GlyphsInfo, commit b2a1b292),
   Copyright (c) 2024, Georg Seifert, under the BSD 3-Clause License (below): Glyphs' names for the
   characters (glyph_name). Nothing else of it (no categories, no recipes).
3. Measurements of open-licensed fonts (SIL Open Font License or Apache License, one font per
   family, 667 families): only counts, ratios, and medians (the layout section and its rules, and each
   entry's families, deriving, and most); no outline, glyph, or name of theirs.

Cited, not included: mekkablue's Glyphs-Scripts (Build Glyphs scripts, commit f89ad5fd, under the
Apache License, Version 2.0), whose constants and methods the research compared these recipes with;
the Microsoft Typography character design standards and the Unicode core specification (quoted in
the research only); fontbakery's checks (Apache License, Version 2.0). Nothing of FontLab's own data
(its alias.dat, which states no license) is included or derived from: FreeLab's tools may only read
such files at run time from the user's own installation.

